{"answer":"`small init` was built so a user never has to hand-author small.toml — the request framed it as detecting entry, framework, requirements.txt, and env-var secrets automatically and writing the file, printing one ✓ line per decision, so the user 'never has to know the file format' (m2120). It also pre-fills `[secrets] required` by scanning the entry file for `os.environ[...]`/`os.getenv`/`os.environ.get`, called out as 'the single most useful thing this command can do' (m2120), implemented via the ENV_RE scan in packages/cli/lib/init.js:7-28.

`small deploy` calls init automatically when no small.toml exists (packages/cli/bin/small.js:56) so that, per the original request, 'the common path is still one command' (m2120) — a user shouldn't have to run init separately before deploy in the normal case. If init can't determine the entry, deploy stops with exit 1 rather than guessing (bin/small.js:56-59, lib/init.js:47-48), matching the spec that undetected entries get a one-line fix message instead of a silent failure.

Note: this was reported done and pushed (m2189, m2211) but not yet published to npm at commit 2649258, so a global `small` install wouldn't have `init` until republished (m2211).","citations":[{"kind":"message","message_id":"m2120"},{"kind":"code","path":"packages/cli/lib/init.js","start_line":1,"end_line":48},{"kind":"code","path":"packages/cli/bin/small.js","start_line":50,"end_line":59},{"kind":"message","message_id":"m2189"},{"kind":"message","message_id":"m2211"}]}
